Blupimania: the keys
====================

Most of the game is played with the mouse: click a square to put the
object chosen in the palette there, and use the buttons on the screen.

  Cursor keys     move a radio-controlled Blupi, or move the view
  Keypad 7 9 1 3  move a radio-controlled Blupi diagonally
  Space           show or hide the objects
  F1 to F4        put the palette's object in front of a radio-controlled
                  Blupi
  F5 F6 F7        slow, normal and fast
  F8              fast panorama on or off
  F9              save the game       F10   load it
  Keypad .        pause
  Return          OK                  Backspace   delete
  Esc             back, and quit

Home and F11 (an Amiga keyboard has neither) are buttons on the screen
too; music on or off (F12 on a PC) is in the settings.

The keys every AmiCradle game has on Right Amiga (GFOpenUp's SDL2.module):
Right Amiga + F window or full screen, + P pause, + Q quit, + M free the
mouse pointer, + S a screenshot in the drawer's Screenshots, and Help
shows this file.
